---
import BaseLayout from '../../components/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../../components/PageHero.astro';
import { site } from '../../config/site';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="Privacy policy for the Joe Rossi Umpires Hall of Fame website and its online services."
  canonicalPath="/privacy-policy/"
  breadcrumbs={[{ name: 'Home', path: '/' }, { name: 'Privacy Policy', path: '/privacy-policy/' }]}
>
  <div class="page-shell">
    <PageHero title="Privacy Policy" intro={`How ${site.legalName} handles information connected with the ${site.name} website.`} />
    <section class="section">
      <article class="page-surface prose policy-copy">
        <p><strong>Last updated:</strong> October 12, 2026</p>

        <h2>Who publishes this site</h2>
        <p>This website is published by {site.legalName} for the {site.name}. The organization’s EIN is {site.ein}.</p>

        <h2>Information we may collect</h2>
        <p>The Joe Rossi Umpires Hall of Fame may collect information you choose to provide through contact forms, event inquiries, biography correction requests, photo or historical material submissions, donation or sponsorship questions, and related correspondence.</p>
        <p>Donation, payment, event registration, and sponsorship information may be processed by approved external providers such as Zeffy. Monthly gifts that began through Stripe before donations moved to Zeffy continue to be processed by Stripe. JRHOF.org does not directly collect or store full payment card details.</p>
        <p>The site uses approved analytics and hosting measurement tools: Google Analytics 4 and Microsoft Clarity, both loaded through Google Tag Manager on JRHOF.org, and Cloudflare Web Analytics. These tools may collect technical information such as pages visited, approximate location, device/browser information, referral sources, and interactions with donation, event, contact, or external links. Microsoft Clarity may also provide aggregated heatmaps and session interaction recordings; it masks sensitive content, and the areas that hold Zeffy donation, registration, and sign-up forms are masked from recordings.</p>

        <h2>Donations and event registration through Zeffy</h2>
        <p>Induction banquet registration uses Zeffy, a ticketing platform for nonprofits. The registration form on JRHOF.org is provided by Zeffy and loads from zeffy.com; it can also be opened on Zeffy’s own website. Zeffy collects the purchaser’s name, email address, location, and optional phone number and seating request, and for each guest a first and last name and a meal choice, with optional email, phone, and dietary needs or allergies. Payment details go directly to Zeffy and its payment processor; the Hall of Fame never receives card or bank numbers.</p>
        <p>The Hall of Fame uses registration information to prepare the guest list, seating, meal counts, check-in, receipts, and event communications, and may share guest names, meal counts, and dietary needs with the event venue for meal service. Dietary information is optional and is used only for meal service. Zeffy sends receipts and e-tickets by email and handles its information under the <a href="https://support.zeffy.com/privacy-policy-5tndw" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Zeffy privacy policy</a>. At checkout Zeffy asks for an optional contribution to Zeffy itself, which you can set to $0; that contribution goes to Zeffy, not to the Hall of Fame.</p>
        <p>The donation form on the Donate page is also provided by Zeffy and loads from zeffy.com. Zeffy collects the information it needs to process a gift and send a tax receipt, such as the donor’s name, email address and payment details, and any optional dedication in honor or in memory of someone. The same Zeffy privacy policy and optional contribution apply.</p>
        <p>On the registration and donation pages, the site records when a form reaches its payment step and when a registration or donation is completed so the Hall of Fame can count them, including those that come from its Google Ad Grants advertising. These events contain no names, contact details, amounts, or payment information.</p>

        <h2 id="newsletter">Email news sign-up</h2>
        <p>The “Stay in the loop” sign-up form on the home, events, and donate pages is provided by Zeffy and loads from zeffy.com only when it scrolls into view or you choose to open it. It asks for your first name, last name, and email address, and adds you to the Hall of Fame’s email list in Zeffy. The Hall of Fame uses that list only to email news about inductions and events, and does not sell or rent it. You can unsubscribe anytime using the link in any of those emails or by asking through the <a href="/contact/">Contact page</a>.</p>
        <p>The site records that a sign-up happened so the Hall of Fame can count sign-ups, including those that come from its Google Ad Grants advertising. That event contains no name or email address.</p>

        <h2>Google Maps directions</h2>
        <p>Event pages may provide a link to Google Maps for venue directions and a map created with Google Maps’ standard sharing feature. To avoid an unnecessary Google request when someone only opens the event page, the embedded map loads when the venue section approaches the visitor’s screen. At that point—or if the visitor opens the directions link—the browser connects to Google, which may process the destination, IP address, browser information, and any location information the visitor separately chooses to provide under Google’s own terms and privacy policy. JRHOF does not request the visitor’s device location.</p>

        <h2>How information may be used</h2>
        <p>Information may be used to respond to inquiries, review biography or archive corrections, coordinate event questions, process donations, manage event registration, and send email news to people who sign up, through Zeffy, maintain appropriate donor or event records, improve the website, and preserve Hall of Fame records.</p>

        <h2>Payments</h2>
        <p>Online payment information is entered only through Zeffy or another approved PCI-compliant payment processor. JRHOF.org does not request payment card numbers through contact forms or email.</p>

        <h2>Information sharing</h2>
        <p>The organization may share information with service providers that help operate the site, process donations, manage event registration, deliver email, host the website, measure site performance, or support organizational records. Examples may include Zeffy, Stripe (for monthly gifts that began there), Google services, Cloudflare, Microsoft Clarity, an approved transactional email provider, hosting providers, and an event venue for meal service.</p>
        <p>The organization may also share information when needed for legal, compliance, security, or organizational governance purposes. The organization does not sell personal information.</p>

        <h2>Retention</h2>
        <p>The organization may retain submitted information for as long as needed to respond to the inquiry, preserve Hall of Fame records, maintain donor or event records, satisfy operational needs, or meet legal and accounting obligations. Registration records are kept in the organization’s Zeffy account for event operations, receipts, and accounting; dietary notes are needed only until the event.</p>

        <h2>Security</h2>
        <p>The organization intends to use reasonable administrative and technical safeguards for information handled through the website. No website or internet transmission can be guaranteed to be completely secure.</p>

        <h2>Children and minors</h2>
        <p>This site is intended for a general audience and does not knowingly seek personal information from children. If a parent or guardian believes a minor has submitted personal information, they may contact the organization through the contact page.</p>

        <h2>External links</h2>
        <p>The site may link to external websites, including CHSBUA, Zeffy, event resources, or historical materials. The organization is not responsible for the privacy practices of external sites.</p>

        <h2>Questions</h2>
        <p>For privacy questions or requests, use the <a href="/contact/">Contact page</a>. Do not send payment card numbers or sensitive financial information through the contact form.</p>
      </article>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .policy-copy { margin-inline: auto; }
</style>
